{
  "type": "minecraft:notice",
  "title": "TNT & Explosions",
  "external_title": "TNT & Explosions",
  "body": [
    {
      "type": "minecraft:plain_message",
      "contents": {
        "text": "TNT & Explosions",
        "bold": true,
        "color": "dark_green"
      },
      "width": 500
    },
    {
      "type": "minecraft:plain_message",
      "contents": {
        "text": "                                                      ",
        "underlined": true,
        "color": "gray"
      },
      "width": 500
    },
    {
      "type": "minecraft:plain_message",
      "contents": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "bold": false,
          "color": "gold"
        },
        {
          "text": "Explosion Protection",
          "bold": true,
          "color": "gold"
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "text": "Explosion block damage is disabled on Pandamium, explosive blocks and entities only do entity damage.",
          "color": "gray"
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "text": "This protects players and their builds from mass griefing caused by explosions and withers.",
          "color": "gray"
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "text": "Will Explosions Be Re-enabled?",
          "bold": true,
          "color": "gold"
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "text": "We have not found a satisfying and safe way to reintroduce explosion block damage yet.",
          "color": "gray"
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "text": "It is something the staff are aware that players want, but protecting newer players' bases remains important.",
          "color": "gray"
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "text": "Alternative Block-Breaking Farms",
          "bold": true,
          "color": "gold"
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "text": "If you need an automated way to break blocks, you can push blocks into a wither while it fires a skull.",
          "color": "gray"
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "text": "This can break blocks instantly and is possible in vanilla Minecraft.",
          "color": "gray"
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "text": "Additionally in Pandamium Crying Obsidian cannot be broken by withers, and wither skulls cannot pass through water making the process of building such farms easier.",
          "color": "gray"
        }
      ],
      "width": 500
    },
    {
      "type": "minecraft:plain_message",
      "contents": {
        "text": "                                                      ",
        "underlined": true,
        "color": "gray"
      },
      "width": 500
    }
  ],
  "can_close_with_escape": true,
  "pause": false,
  "after_action": "none",
  "action": {
    "label": {
      "translate": "gui.back"
    },
    "action": {
      "type": "minecraft:run_command",
      "command": "trigger help set 3"
    }
  }
}
